---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "September 11, 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Dinkly"
  description="Dinkly's privacy policy: no accounts, no email collection, and no personal data sold. What we store, what we don't, and how advertising cookies work."
>
  <div class="wrap narrow page">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> <span>Privacy Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="head">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        The short version: Dinkly has no accounts, collects no email addresses, and does not sell personal
        information. Everything you do on this site — quiz results, game scores, your daily card — stays in
        your own browser.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information we do not collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No account registration, and therefore no names, passwords or phone numbers.</li>
        <li>No email addresses, and no newsletter or mailing list of any kind.</li>
        <li>No contact lists, camera, microphone or precise location access.</li>
        <li>No upload of quiz answers, game results, oracle questions or draw history to our servers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Information stored in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        Some features remember you between visits using <strong>local storage</strong> — a mechanism that
        keeps data on your own device. Dinkly currently stores:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your best Dink Match time and move count.</li>
        <li>The result of your most recent personality quiz, so we can avoid re-asking.</li>
        <li>Interface preferences, if any are added.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        None of this is transmitted to us. Clearing your browser's site data for this domain removes all of it.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Server logs and hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served as static files by a content delivery network. Like almost all web hosting, our
        provider may automatically record standard technical information such as IP address, request time,
        requested URL, referrer and user-agent string, in aggregate logs used for security and abuse
        prevention. We do not use these logs to identify individuals.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Dinkly is free and supported by advertising. We use third-party advertising partners, currently
        including <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. These partners may:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use cookies or similar identifiers to serve and measure advertising.</li>
        <li>Serve personalised advertising based on prior visits to this and other websites.</li>
        <li>Collect device and approximate location information for ad delivery and fraud prevention.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visit to
        this site and other sites on the internet. You may opt out of personalised advertising through
        Google's <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Ads Settings</a>,
        or opt out of third-party vendor cookies at
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Directly sold placements on this site are labelled <em>Sponsored</em>. We do not run pop-ups,
        interstitials, or audio advertising inside our ambient sound player.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        If analytics tooling is enabled, it is used only in aggregate to understand which pages are useful.
        It is not used to build individual profiles, and it is not linked to any identifying information.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Children</h2>
      <p>
        Dinkly is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information
        from children. Because we do not collect personal information from anyone, there is nothing to
        delete on request — but if you believe a child's data has been captured by an advertising partner,
        contact us and we will investigate.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or restrict processing
        of your personal data, and to object to personalised advertising. Because we do not hold personal
        data about you, the practical route for advertising-related requests is directly through our
        advertising partners' own controls (see section 4).
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially — for example if we add accounts or a newsletter — the change will
        be reflected here with an updated date, and it will be described plainly rather than buried.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy can be raised through the <a href="/about/">About page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: 780px; }
  .page { padding: 34px 0 20px; }
  .crumbs { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--faint); display: flex; gap: 8px; }
  .crumbs a { color: var(--muted); }
  .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .head { margin: 28px 0 30px; }
  .head h1 { font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 46px); margin-bottom: 10px; }

  .prose { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.76; }
  .prose .lead { font-size: 18px; color: var(--muted); }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 36px 0 12px; }
  .prose p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .prose ul { margin: 0 0 16px; padding-left: 22px; }
  .prose li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .prose a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 500; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, transparent); }
</style>
